#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:5
#: 20392f3e9eac4ae996f8e6d8b300aaac
msgid "Clock/Time Synchronisation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:7
#: 0539890a658347f59a57d3214c2f6227
msgid "The flight controller and companion computer clocks can be synchronised using MAVLink's `SYSTEM_TIME <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SYSTEM_TIME>`__ and `TIMESYNC <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#TIMESYNC>`__ messages.  This is important so that each side can blend data from the other side into its EKF."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:9
#: 1a2ceb823c324e49b20627a19f1786f6
msgid "`mavros's sys_time plugin <https://github.com/mavlink/mavros/blob/master/mavros/src/plugins/sys_time.cpp>`__ implements the mavros/ROS side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:10
#: 49d604c89ceb43c194c84e028a17955b
msgid "ArduPilot's `AP_RTC <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/AP_RTC>`__ library implements the ArduPilot side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:13
#: bf7312ce8ef242049c4c225006b7e3de
msgid "Mavros Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:15
#: c22f7855c58d4c2f96557d0eafcbcf46
msgid "Mavros's `apm_config.yaml <https://github.com/mavlink/mavros/blob/master/mavros/launch/apm_config.yaml>`__ file can be modified to configure the rate of the `SYSTEM_TIME <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SYSTEM_TIME>`__ and `TIMESYNC <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#TIMESYNC>`__ messages.  Below are the recommended settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:27
#: de62c0e372114495851aa83317cbac4b
msgid "ArduPilot Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:29
#: e52756318aae4b22b9b4d7aa3ec1a747
msgid "The flight controller's time is set from the GPS by default but can be set from one of three sources(GPS, MAVLINK, onboard HW clock) using the :ref:`BRD_RTC_TYPES <BRD_RTC_TYPES>` parameter as a bit mask for the time synchronisation source. When using mavros set ``BRD_RTC_TYPES`` = 2 to only allow the \"MAVLINK_SYSTEM_TIME\" source which uses the `SYSTEM_TIME <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#SYSTEM_TIME>`__ MAVLINK message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:31
#: 2c7191ff71b547b8872eb15a0b186a86
msgid "If the ``RTT too high for timesync`` message is shown in the Mavros console (most commonly when using ArduRover), the :ref:`SCHED_LOOP_RATE <SCHED_LOOP_RATE>` parameter should be increased. This is because Mavros ignores TIMESYNC messages if the round trip time is more than 10ms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:34
#: ee0dad45b2be452aa492f91e73d1581a
msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ros-timesync.rst:36
#: 4212e497c8a94cd3913f23e8f03e95b2
msgid "A MAVLink inspector (available using QGC or MissionPlanner) can be used to check that the system times are synchronised.  If using Mission Planner, press Ctrl-F and push the \"MAVLink Inspector\" button."
msgstr ""
